  "question": {
    "text": "Consider three observations <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>c</mi></math> such that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></math>. If the standard deviation of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>d</mi></math>,&nbsp;then which of the following is true?"
